COMMIT 7ccbaadbb04d0bbfcdcc2d729aff400ad4253943
docs(core): say that park can throw before it returns a future

Three text defects left by FIX-142's two review rounds, all in the two
files it touched, none blocking on its own.

(a) Parking.park's javadoc promised what a failing or throwing persist
does, but never said that park itself can throw SYNCHRONOUSLY: its first
statement is Parked.of(...), which reads failure.toString(). That throw
is the reason FIX-142 exists, and a caller reading the javadoc would not
have expected it.

(b) The width comment cited D-104 where D-111 is the closer precedent.
Both are cited now, D-111 first. The implementer found the same stale
citation in persist's comment and fixed it too, rather than leaving the
two comments to disagree about the same question.

(c) The test comment named the wrong line for where the Error escaped
the assertion machinery.

(c) is the one worth recording, because the packet was wrong about it.
It told the implementer to point the comment at the assertSame. The
implementer compiled a probe against junit-jupiter-api 5.14.4 and
opentest4j 1.3.0 and found that a Throwable fills its stack trace at
CONSTRUCTION, so the topmost frame is the new Error(...) line and no
frame names the assertSame at all. It corrected the instruction instead
of obeying it, and the reviewer confirmed the finding from the recorded
red log. The comment now anchors to a name, not a number.

Evidence: ParkingTest 22/22, BUILD SUCCESS. No mutants are owed and none
were invented: a comment-only diff changes no bytecode. The module
verify run spent on this change tested nothing it was bought for, since
there is no maven-javadoc-plugin in any pom and -Xlint does not resolve
{@link} references; that is now in agent/NOTES.md.

Also recorded, both found by the reviewer outside its own task: FIX-151,
an unprintable step failure concatenated into FlowWorker's WARNING on
the branch that has no Throwable catch above it, and FIX-152, stale line
citations in the ledgers.

